From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp20x: clear the BSP boot flag on power off

The GA36-MB boots with Allwinner's BSP u-boot, which keeps a flag in the
AXP22x data buffer register 0x0f. It writes 0x0e on every boot. When a
charger brings the PMIC up, it shows its charger screen only if the
flag is not 0x0e; otherwise it assumes the system was running and boots
it. The BSP kernel writes 0x00 there on power off. Mainline never touches
it, so plugging a charger into a powered off console boots the OS.

Clear the flag before cutting the power on AXP221/AXP223.

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c b/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
@@ -1252,6 +1252,10 @@
 		shutdown_reg = AXP20X_OFF_CTRL;
 		break;
 	}
+
+	/* the BSP u-boot skips its charger screen while this holds 0x0e */
+	if (axp20x->variant == AXP221_ID || axp20x->variant == AXP223_ID)
+		regmap_write(axp20x->regmap, AXP20X_DATACACHE(11), 0);
 
 	regmap_write(axp20x->regmap, shutdown_reg, AXP20X_OFF);
 
